# Global React Project Conventions (SHM)

You are working on the **SHM** React + TypeScript codebase (Vite, Tailwind, Shadcn UI).

**Core principles:**

- 1 folder = 1 responsibility
- Keep components small: split if >250 lines; hooks/utils ≤150 lines
- Co-locate related files (styles, tests, types) next to the component when applicable
- Max 3–4 levels of folder nesting
- Use consistent naming — never deviate (see naming-conventions.mdc)
- Separate concerns: UI → components, logic → hooks, data → api/utils/types
- Make everything searchable: descriptive, unique, predictable names

**Top-level src/ structure (this project):**

```bash
├── src/
  ├── App/           # Root app and router (App/index.tsx)
  ├── api/           # API client, endpoints (constants only), index
  ├── components/
  │   ├── ui/        # Shadcn primitives (button, card, etc.)
  │   ├── layout/    # header, sidebar, footer
  │   └── features/  # feature-specific components (timeline/, golden-temple/, ten-gurus/)
  ├── contexts/      # e.g. auth-context
  ├── constants/     # routes, app-wide constants
  ├── hooks/         # useAPI, feature hooks, feature/use-*-page.ts
  ├── pages/         # Thin page components only
  ├── schemas/       # Zod (and similar) validation schemas
  ├── styles/        # global CSS
  ├── types/         # shared TS types
  └── utils/         # pure helpers, auth-utils (no API URLs)
```

**Folder names:** always **lowercase-kebab-case** (exception: top-level `App/`).

**Path alias:** Use `@/` for src (e.g. `@/components/ui/button`, `@/api`, `@/hooks/useApi`). Never use deep relative paths like `../../../components`.

## Data fetching

- **No TanStack Query** – Do not use `QueryClient`, `useQuery`, or `useMutation`.
- **All API calls** go through **`useAPI`** (`src/hooks/useApi.ts`) or a feature hook that uses `useAPI`. Endpoints come from `API_ENDPOINTS` in `src/api/endpoints.ts` (constants only).
- Feature hooks (e.g. `useSikhApps`, `useTimeline`) live in `src/hooks/` and call `useAPI` with the appropriate endpoint and options.

## State

- **Server/API state:** `useAPI` (and feature hooks built on it)
- **Local UI state:** React state/hooks (useState, useReducer)
- **Auth state:** `AuthContext` + `auth-utils` (token, logout)
- No global client store (no Zustand/Redux) in this project

## Screens (pages)

- **Pages are thin:** A page file only composes a **page hook** (e.g. `useTimelinePage`) and **feature components**; no large inline state or JSX. See **screen-architecture.mdc** for screen creation and modification.
